{
  "message": "I’m here to help. “No Service” usually points to one of a few causes: Airplane Mode ON, a SIM issue, incorrect network settings, weak coverage in your area, or an account/line suspension. My plan is: (1) identify your account to check your line status, then (2) walk you through a couple of quick device checks to restore service as fast as possible.",
  "request": {
    "identify": "Please provide one of the following so I can find your account and the affected line: (a) the phone number of the line with No Service, or (b) your customer ID, or (c) your full name plus date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD).",
    "questions": [
      "Are you currently traveling outside your usual area (or outside the country)?",
      "Is anyone else on your account seeing issues right now?",
      "Roughly where are you located (city/area) so I can consider local coverage?"
    ]
  },
  "while_we_verify": {
    "quick_checks": [
      "Status bar check: Please look at the top of your screen and tell me exactly what you see for (a) Airplane Mode icon, (b) signal bars (or “No Service”), and (c) network type (5G/4G/LTE/3G).",
      "Airplane Mode: If you see it ON, please turn it OFF and wait 10 seconds. If it’s already OFF, toggle Airplane Mode ON for 10 seconds, then OFF again.",
      "SIM status: In Settings > Mobile/Cellular > SIMs (wording varies), does it show your SIM/eSIM as active, missing, or locked (PIN/PUK)? If unsure, try reseating the physical SIM (power off, remove SIM, reinsert, power on)."
    ],
    "notes": "These steps help rule out the most common causes quickly. Once I locate your account, I’ll also check for any suspension or network/roaming settings that could explain the outage."
  }
}

