  "thought_process": "You’re currently connected on 2G while abroad. MMS needs at least 3G, ideally 4G/5G. Since I’ve enabled roaming on your line, the next steps are to make your phone prefer 4G/5G and then re-register to the network. If it still sticks to 2G, we’ll check APN/MMSC and a couple of phone settings that can interfere.",
  "do_this_next_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Set network mode to prefer faster networks",
      "why": "Forces the phone to seek 4G/5G instead of staying on 2G.",
      "how": "Use set_network_mode_preference to select \"4g_5g_preferred\"."
    },
    {
      "step": "Force a fresh network registration",
      "why": "Helps the phone latch onto a better roaming network.",
      "how": "Use toggle_airplane_mode to turn ON for ~20 seconds, then OFF."
    },
    {
      "step": "Re-check connection and test",
      "why": "Confirm you’re off 2G and that data works.",
      "how": [
        "Look at the status bar for 4G/LTE/5G and at least fair signal.",
        "Try loading a simple webpage.",
        "Try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "if_still_on_2g_or_mms_fails": [
    {
      "step": "Reboot the phone",
      "why": "Full refresh of radios and settings.",
      "how": "Use reboot_device."
    },
    {
      "step": "Verify APN/MMSC",
      "why": "MMS depends on a correct MMSC URL in APN.",
      "how": [
        "Use check_apn_settings. If MMSC is missing/incorrect, use reset_apn_settings.",
        "After resetting APN, use reboot_device before testing again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn off Wi‑Fi Calling temporarily",
      "why": "In some cases it interferes with MMS while roaming.",
      "how": "Use check_wifi_calling_status, and if it’s ON, use toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF. Test MMS."
    },
    {
      "step": "Make sure Data Saver and VPN aren’t limiting data",
      "why": "Both can disrupt or slow MMS/data.",
      "how": [
        "Use check_data_restriction_status; if Data Saver is ON, use toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF.",
        "Use check_vpn_status; if connected, use disconnect_vpn."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_report_back": [
    "After step 1–2: what does the status bar show now (network type and signal)?",
    "Can you load a simple webpage after these steps?",
    "Does the MMS send now? If not, what changed, if anything?"
  ],
  "question": "Do you know if your phone is Android or iPhone? If you tell me, I can tailor the on-screen menu steps for set_network_mode_preference and the other checks.",
  "note": "If the phone remains stuck on 2G after these steps, MMS won’t work on 2G. We can keep troubleshooting, but you may need to move to an area with better signal where 3G/4G/5G is available."
}

