messages.content:
{
  "thought_process": "Your line is active on our side. Since Airplane Mode is now OFF but you still see No Signal, the most likely causes are a SIM recognition/seat issue or the phone preferring an incompatible network mode. We’ll verify the SIM’s status first, reseat it if needed, then ensure the network mode is set correctly.",
  "do_this_now": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "title": "Check SIM status",
      "how_to": "Use the SIM check on your phone (check_sim_status).",
      "what_to_look_for": "Report back whether it shows Active, Missing/Not detected, or Locked (PIN/PUK).",
      "why": "If the SIM isn’t detected or is locked, the phone cannot register on the network."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "If SIM is Missing/Not detected — reseat it",
      "how_to": "Run reseat_sim_card (remove and reinsert the SIM carefully), then power back on if the phone powers off during the process.",
      "why": "A slightly misaligned SIM often causes persistent No Signal."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "title": "If SIM is Locked — stop and tell me",
      "how_to": "Do not guess PIN/PUK. Tell me exactly what it shows.",
      "why": "Incorrect entries can permanently block the SIM; I’ll escalate appropriately."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "Confirm preferred network mode",
      "how_to": "Check your phone’s network mode (check_network_mode_preference). If it’s not already modern (4G/5G), set it to 4g_5g_preferred (set_network_mode_preference).",
      "why": "Older modes (2G/3G) can prevent registration or be unavailable in many areas."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "title": "Wait for registration",
      "how_to": "After the above, wait 60 seconds and watch the status bar for signal bars/4G/5G.",
      "why": "The device needs a moment to reattach to the network."
    }
  ],
  "optional_next_if_still_no_signal": [
    {
      "step": 6,
      "title": "APN quick check",
      "how_to": "Check APN settings (check_apn_settings). If they show incorrect/missing values, reset to default (reset_apn_settings) and then reboot the phone (reboot_device).",
      "why": "Incorrect network settings can interfere with proper registration and data."
    }
  ],
  "request": "Please run step 1 (check_sim_status) and tell me exactly what it shows. If it’s Missing, go ahead with step 2 (reseat_sim_card) before reporting back. Also let me know what your network mode shows so I can confirm it’s set to 4g_5g_preferred.",
  "notes": "If you’re not sure how to access these on your device, tell me whether you’re on iPhone or Android and your phone model, and I’ll tailor the taps. I’m standing by for your SIM status result."
}

