messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the update. MMS generally will not work on 2G. Your line is Active and under the data limit, so the next step is to get your phone on a faster network type (4G/5G), then re-test. We’ll also verify APN/MMSC and a couple of app/device settings if needed.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Switch network mode to prefer 4G/5G",
      "what_to_do": "Use set_network_mode_preference with mode \"4g_5g_preferred\".",
      "how": "On most phones: Settings > Mobile Network/Cellular > Network mode/Preferred network type > choose 5G/4G/LTE (Auto).",
      "then": "Wait ~15–30 seconds for the status bar to show 4G/LTE/5G and at least fair signal."
    },
    {
      "title": "Quick connectivity test",
      "what_to_do": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF for now and ensure Mobile Data is ON.",
        "Place a quick test call and send a regular SMS.",
        "Open a simple website (e.g., example.com)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Test MMS again",
      "what_to_do": "Send a single small photo to your own number and note exactly what happens (e.g., stuck on “Sending…”, “Failed to send”)."
    },
    {
      "title": "If you’re still stuck on 2G or MMS still fails",
      "what_to_do": [
        "Run check_apn_settings and share the APN name and whether an MMSC URL is present.",
        "If MMSC is missing/incorrect: use reset_apn_settings, then use reboot_device.",
        "Run check_wifi_calling_status; if Wi‑Fi Calling is ON, use toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF temporarily and try MMS again.",
        "Run check_app_permissions for your messaging app; if “storage” and “sms” aren’t granted, use grant_app_permission for each.",
        "If you’re traveling outside your usual area/country, ensure data roaming is ON on the phone (use toggle_roaming to enable)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "requests": {
    "device_details": [
      "Phone make/model and whether it’s Android or iPhone (and version if you know it).",
      "Which messaging app you’re using (e.g., Messages/Google Messages/Samsung Messages)."
    ],
    "after_step_1_2_3": [
      "Run check_network_status and/or check_status_bar and paste the full output (signal strength, network type, mobile data ON/OFF, roaming ON/OFF).",
      "Did the call connect and did the SMS send?",
      "Did the website load on mobile data?",
      "What exactly happens when sending the MMS now?"
    ],
    "traveling": "Are you currently traveling outside your usual area/country?"
  },
  "why_these_steps": "MMS requires at least 3G and active mobile data. Moving from 2G to 4G/5G addresses the most likely cause. If it still fails, incorrect APN/MMSC, Wi‑Fi Calling conflicts, or missing app permissions are common culprits. We’ll verify each in turn."
}

