  "acknowledgement": "Thanks for the detailed update. Your phone reporting “SIM missing” explains the no‑service/no‑data and the MMS failure. Our goal now is to get the SIM recognized.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs mobile data. A missing SIM prevents any network attachment. The correct path is: confirm SIM status, reseat the SIM if it’s missing, then reboot and re-test. If the SIM shows locked, we must escalate for PIN/PUK. If it remains missing after reseat and reboot, it likely indicates a SIM or SIM-slot fault and we’ll escalate for replacement.",
  "questions_before_steps": "Do you use a physical SIM card (tray you can eject) or an eSIM (no tray)? If you’re unsure, check the phone’s edge for a tiny pinhole tray.",
  "steps_now": [
    {
      "step": "1) Since the phone shows SIM = Missing, reseat the SIM (for physical SIM only).",
      "instructions": [
        "Power the phone OFF.",
        "Eject the SIM tray, remove the SIM, gently wipe the gold contacts, and reinsert it flush and snug.",
        "Reinsert the tray and power the phone ON."
      ],
      "note": "If you have an eSIM (no tray), skip this step."
    },
    {
      "step": "2) Reboot the device (required).",
      "instructions": [
        "After reseating (or if using eSIM), restart the phone once."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "3) Re-check service and test MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF.",
        "Look at the status bar: do you now see signal bars and a network type like 4G/LTE/5G?",
        "Try loading example.com in the browser.",
        "Then try sending an MMS again."
      ],
      "what_to_report": "Tell me if the SIM status still says Missing, if it shows Locked/PIN required, or if service and data returned."
    }
  ],
  "branching_outcomes": [
    {
      "condition": "If SIM shows Locked/PIN/PUK required",
      "action": "I will transfer you to a human agent to assist with SIM security (PIN/PUK)."
    },
    {
      "condition": "If SIM still shows Missing after reseat + reboot (or you’re on eSIM and it still shows Missing)",
      "action": "This points to a SIM or SIM-slot/profile issue. I will transfer you to a human agent to arrange a replacement or further diagnostics."
    }
  ],
  "next": "Please confirm whether you have a physical SIM or eSIM, proceed with the steps above, and share exactly what you see after the reboot (SIM status, signal indicator, and whether a webpage loads/MMS sends). I’ll guide you from there."
}

