messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for checking. “No Signal” + “Data Disabled” means your phone currently isn’t connected to the cellular network and mobile data is OFF, so MMS can’t work yet. Let’s bring service and data back step by step.",
  "thought_process": "We just refueled your plan, so the remaining blockers are on-device: Airplane Mode, SIM recognition, mobile data switch, or network mode. We’ll rule them out in order from quickest to most impactful.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "why": "Airplane Mode disables all radios and shows no signal.",
      "do_this": [
        "Use check_status_bar to see if ✈️ Airplane Mode is showing.",
        "If it is, use toggle_airplane_mode to turn it OFF.",
        "Wait ~10 seconds and check if signal bars appear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "why": "Mobile data must be ON for MMS.",
      "do_this": [
        "Use check_network_status to confirm Mobile Data status.",
        "If it shows Data Disabled, use toggle_data to turn mobile data ON."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "why": "If there’s still no signal, the phone may not see the SIM.",
      "do_this": [
        "Use check_sim_status.",
        "If it says Missing, use reseat_sim_card (this simulates removing/reinserting).",
        "If it says Locked (PIN/PUK), tell me—I'll transfer you to a specialist for SIM unlock.",
        "If it says Active, proceed to Step 4."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "why": "For best connectivity and MMS, your phone should prefer 4G/5G.",
      "do_this": [
        "Use check_network_mode_preference.",
        "If it’s 2G/3G, use set_network_mode_preference with \"4g_5g_preferred\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "why": "A reboot refreshes all radios and applies network setting changes.",
      "do_this": [
        "Use reboot_device.",
        "After the reboot, wait ~30 seconds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "why": "Verify service and data are back, then confirm MMS.",
      "do_this": [
        "Use check_status_bar: you should see signal bars and 📱 Data Enabled.",
        "Optionally run run_speed_test (anything above ‘unknown/no connection’ confirms data).",
        "Try sending an MMS (e.g., a photo) to yourself."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "please_reply_with": [
    "Whether Airplane Mode was ON or OFF and its current status.",
    "Whether you were able to turn Mobile Data ON.",
    "SIM status result (Active/Missing/Locked).",
    "Current network mode preference (and if you changed it).",
    "What you see in the status bar after the reboot (signal bars? Data Enabled?).",
    "Whether the MMS sent successfully."
  ],
  "notes": "If at any step you see errors or unclear results, tell me exactly what you see and we’ll adjust. Once we have signal and data enabled, MMS should send normally."
}

