{
  "message": "Great—since mobile data works well but MMS still won’t send, the most likely causes are MMS server settings (APN/MMSC), Wi‑Fi Calling interaction, Data Saver/VPN interference, or missing app permissions. Let’s fix these in order.",
  "steps_now": [
    {
      "title": "Reset APN/MMSC to default (most common MMS fix when roaming)",
      "instructions": [
        "On Android: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Access Point Names.",
        "Tap the menu (⋮) > Reset to default (or Reset APNs).",
        "Important: Restart your phone after the reset (power off/on)."
      ],
      "why": "This restores the correct MMSC server address your phone uses to send MMS."
    },
    {
      "title": "Test MMS after reboot",
      "instructions": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF for the test.",
        "Ensure Mobile Data and Data Roaming are ON.",
        "Send a photo MMS to your own number and wait up to 1–2 minutes."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "if_still_fails_after_apn_reset": [
    {
      "title": "Turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling temporarily",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Wi‑Fi Calling > OFF"
      ],
      "why": "Some configurations block MMS while roaming."
    },
    {
      "title": "Ensure Data Saver is OFF",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver > OFF"
      ],
      "why": "Data Saver can restrict MMS background transfer."
    },
    {
      "title": "Disconnect any VPN",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > VPN > Disconnect"
      ],
      "why": "A VPN can interfere with MMS routing."
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirm messaging app permissions",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Apps > Messages (your default app) > Permissions.",
        "Allow: SMS and Photos/Media (or Files and media)."
      ],
      "why": "The app needs SMS and media access to send MMS."
    },
    {
      "title": "Test again",
      "instructions": [
        "With Wi‑Fi still OFF and Mobile Data + Data Roaming ON, send a photo MMS to your own number."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "optional_check": [
    {
      "title": "Preferred network type",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Preferred network type > choose 4G/5G."
      ],
      "why": "Avoids falling back to 2G/3G which can break MMS."
    }
  ],
  "request_update": "Please start with the APN reset + reboot and run the MMS test. If it still fails, work through the follow-up items (Wi‑Fi Calling OFF, Data Saver OFF, VPN off, permissions) and test again. Tell me exactly what happens (sends successfully, stuck on sending, or any error).",
