messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thank you for sticking with this—I know it’s frustrating. You already did the big fixes (added data, turned off Airplane Mode, reset APN, restarted). The most common remaining causes are phone settings that block MMS. I’ll explain each next step and why it helps, and we can go one tap at a time. None of these steps will delete or change your photos.",
  "what_we_already_did": [
    "Confirmed your line is active and refueled 2 GB of data.",
    "Turned off Airplane Mode.",
    "Tested with Wi‑Fi off.",
    "Reset APN to default and restarted."
  ],
  "next_steps_and_why": [
    {
      "step": "Check network type and prefer 4G/5G",
      "why": "MMS won’t reliably send on 2G/3G. We want the phone to prefer 4G/5G.",
      "how": [
        "Look at the top of your screen for 4G/LTE/5G next to the signal bars.",
        "If you don’t see 4G/LTE/5G: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Preferred network type > choose 5G/4G/LTE (sometimes called 4G/5G preferred).",
        "Try sending the picture again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn Wi‑Fi Calling OFF",
      "why": "Some devices block MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Wi‑Fi Calling > turn OFF.",
        "Return to Messages and try sending the picture again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Make sure Data Saver is OFF",
      "why": "Data Saver can block background data that MMS needs.",
      "how": [
        "Quick Settings: look for Data Saver and turn it OFF.",
        "Or Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver > OFF.",
        "Try the picture again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Disconnect any VPN",
      "why": "VPNs can interfere with MMS routing.",
      "how": [
        "If you see a key icon at the top of the screen, a VPN is on.",
        "Settings > Network & Internet > VPN > disconnect or turn OFF.",
        "Try the picture again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Confirm Messaging app permissions",
      "why": "The Messages app must have permission to access media and send SMS/MMS.",
      "how": [
        "Settings > Apps > Messages (your texting app) > Permissions.",
        "Allow: Files and media (or Photos and videos) and SMS.",
        "Open Messages and try the picture again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Run an MMS diagnostic (optional but helpful)",
      "why": "This quickly tells us if the phone thinks it can send MMS.",
      "how": [
        "If your phone offers Diagnostics, open it and run the MMS test (called Can send MMS).",
        "Tell me what it reports (pass/fail or any message)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "reassurance": "All of these steps only change connection settings and permissions. They will not affect or delete your photos.",
  "let_me_walk_you_through": "If you prefer, we can do this together one screen at a time. Reply “ready” and tell me which Settings screen you see, and I’ll give you the next tap.",
  "questions": [
    "Would you like to start with checking Preferred network type now?",
    "Do you see a switch for Wi‑Fi Calling in Mobile network, and if so, can you turn it OFF?",
    "Do you see Data Saver or a VPN icon (a small key) at the top?"
  ],
  "what_happens_if_still_failing": "If it still won’t send after we complete these checks, I’ll summarize everything we tried and transfer you to a human specialist for deeper diagnostics."
}

