messages.content:
{
  "message": "Your data connection looks good (5G, excellent signal), so MMS is likely being blocked by configuration on the phone. We’ll rule out Wi‑Fi Calling/VPN conflicts, then verify the Messages app has the right permissions. If needed, we’ll refresh APN settings and reboot.",
  "keep_wifi_off_for_tests": true,
  "steps_in_order": [
    {
      "step": "Check Wi‑Fi Calling",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_wifi_calling_status.",
        "If it shows Wi‑Fi Calling is ON, use toggle_wifi_calling to turn it OFF.",
        "Try sending the MMS again with Wi‑Fi still OFF."
      ],
      "why": "Some carriers don’t support MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling or it can interfere while roaming."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check VPN",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_vpn_status.",
        "If a VPN is connected, use disconnect_vpn.",
        "Retry the MMS."
      ],
      "why": "A VPN can disrupt MMS routing even when general web browsing works."
    },
    {
      "step": "Confirm app permissions",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\").",
        "If storage or sms permissions are NOT granted, run:",
        "grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"storage\")",
        "grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"sms\")",
        "Force close and reopen the Messages app, then retry the MMS."
      ],
      "why": "The Messages app needs storage (for media) and SMS permissions to send MMS."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check Data Saver",
      "actions": [
        "Run check_data_restriction_status.",
        "If Data Saver is ON, use toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF.",
        "Retry the MMS."
      ],
      "why": "Data Saver can restrict background data that MMS depends on."
    },
    {
      "step": "APN/MMSC refresh (only if still failing)",
      "actions": [
        "Even though your MMSC is set, use reset_apn_settings to ensure the full APN profile is correct.",
        "Then run reboot_device.",
        "After reboot: confirm Mobile Data = ON and Data Roaming = ON, keep Wi‑Fi OFF, and try sending the MMS again."
      ],
      "why": "A subtle APN mismatch can block MMS while regular data works. Resetting + reboot reliably fixes this."
    },
    {
      "step": "Capability check (if needed)",
      "actions": [
        "If it still fails, run can_send_mms and tell me the result string."
      ],
      "why": "This helps pinpoint if the device/app still reports an MMS capability issue."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_share_back": [
    "Wi‑Fi Calling status (ON or OFF) and whether turning it OFF helped.",
    "VPN status and whether disconnecting it helped.",
    "Which permissions the messaging app had, and what you granted.",
    "Whether Data Saver was ON.",
    "If you performed the APN reset + reboot and the result when retrying MMS.",
    "If you ran can_send_mms, the exact result."
  ],
  "thought_process": "With strong 5G and working web, MMS failures usually come down to Wi‑Fi Calling/VPN interference, missing app permissions, or APN profile quirks. Working through these in order should restore MMS.",
  "request": "Please start with Wi‑Fi Calling and VPN checks, then permissions, and let me know the outcomes. I’m ready to keep guiding you step by step based on what you find."
}

