{
  "response": "Thanks for the update. Since MMS needs mobile data and you’re abroad, we’ll first make sure Mobile Data and Data Roaming are enabled on the phone. Your screen showing “No Signal” means the phone hasn’t registered on a network yet; enabling these and preferring modern networks usually helps the phone latch on. I’ll guide you one small step at a time.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — Turn Mobile Data ON",
      "why": "MMS requires mobile data. This won’t harm anything and is reversible.",
      "instructions": [
        "a) Swipe down from the top of the screen twice to fully open Quick Settings.",
        "b) Find the Mobile data tile and tap it so it turns ON (highlighted).",
        "If you don’t see the tile: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs) > toggle Mobile data ON."
      ],
      "report_back": [
        "Confirm Mobile Data shows ON in Quick Settings or Settings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — Turn Data Roaming ON (since you’re in France)",
      "why": "Without Data Roaming, your phone won’t use data on foreign networks, and MMS won’t work.",
      "instructions": [
        "a) Go to Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections).",
        "b) Tap Mobile network (or SIMs).",
        "c) Turn Data roaming ON."
      ],
      "report_back": [
        "Confirm Data Roaming is ON."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — Prefer 4G/5G networks",
      "why": "Ensures the phone tries to connect to networks that fully support MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "a) Still in Mobile network settings, find Preferred network type.",
        "b) Set it to 4G/5G (or 5G/4G/LTE preferred). Avoid 2G/3G-only options."
      ],
      "report_back": [
        "Tell me what option you selected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Check the status bar",
      "why": "We want to see the phone register on a network.",
      "instructions": [
        "a) Wait 20–30 seconds.",
        "b) Look at the top of the screen and tell me: how many signal bars you see, and whether it now shows 4G/LTE/5G or still says No Signal/Data Disabled.",
        "c) Keep Wi‑Fi OFF for this test."
      ],
      "report_back": [
        "Bars count and any 4G/LTE/5G label, or if it still says No Signal/Data Disabled."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": "Please go through Steps 1–4 and report back what you see after each step (especially Step 4). If it still says No Signal after these, we’ll do a quick, safe reboot to nudge the connection, and if needed we’ll check SIM status next. I’m here with you."
}

